0 FILE sp-crossing-study.ldr
0 Name: C enlarged crossing frame and raised windowed apse (local coordinates)
0 // 4x4 foot pads -> six-brick piers -> orthogonal beam layers -> four 4x4 plates forming an 8x8-stud bearing with top stud plane y=-200.
0 // Lower 2x8-equivalent rails use four contiguous 1x8 bricks at x=+-50/70, crossing 8 transverse 1x8 beams. Every beam is one-piece across its span; no unsupported end-to-end seam.
0 // Apse foot remains at y=0; wall and windows shift +40 Z and rise to eight brick courses. A 4x4 plate at z=80,y=-208 is a calculated tie candidate; only shared stud rows count as contact.
0 // The 8x8 bearing is a comparison envelope, not a final dome diameter or a load-tested support.
