0 FILE sp-colonnade-curve-study.ldr
0 E: curved colonnade comparisons from D’s round piers and flat horizontal lintel. 15° and 30° are local study angles, not a final rule. The 15-degree and 30-degree comparison joints use floor/roof 2429/2430 hinge pairs, corrected 3023b foot/lintel contacts, and two six-brick 3062b round columns each. The added chain reuses a corrected 15-degree joint and adds a second 15-degree joint plus bridging 3020 foot/lintel plates to make three connected straight runs. Local study only; dimensions/colors are not product specifications.
0 15-degree curve-joint sample; local pivot P=(-160,0,0), vertical axis +Y. Base and roof hinges share the same yaw; the two straight leaves are mechanically linked at the hinge.
0 !BRICK_INSTANCE E-00001
