0 Four-pier comparison bay: existing 80 LDU along-row pitch and 60 LDU row spacing. The floor top is Y=-16 and bottom Y=0; beam and roof datums match the established colonnade.
0 Base test: one 2x2 round brick (3941) replaces the equal-height 1x1 plate stack, giving a centered 10 LDU base projection around the thin 1x1 round shaft.
0 Capital test: three 34103 jumpers transfer the shaft center to four balanced 3022 top studs. Their inside-holder geometry is source-mesh checked; physical clutch is not verified.
0 Roof is two connected tiled strips; the 20 LDU middle slot between the 60 LDU-spaced rows remains open.
